{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in today because of worsening pain in your skin wounds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. The pain in my left hip, right breast, and belly got much worse during dialysis. It’s sharp and comes and goes, but it’s worse at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve been dealing with calciphylaxis for a while. The ER team started you on IV antibiotics—clindamycin and cipro—because there’s concern for infection in the wound areas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had that same infection last month. They gave me antibiotics then. Is it back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. The gram stain from your thigh ulcer showed a small amount of bacteria, mostly white blood cells and some gram-positive cocci. It’s not a heavy infection, but we’re treating it to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But the pain is mostly from the calciphylaxis, not just infection, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The calciphylaxis is the main issue—those chalky, firm areas on your skin are calcium deposits. They’re very painful. Dermatology recommends trying intralesional sodium thiosulfate injections once you’re out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I couldn’t tolerate the IV version before—made me vomit. Are the shots better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, these are injections directly into the wounds. They’re usually better tolerated and can help heal the lesions and reduce pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2119-07-13 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m willing to try. Anything to stop this pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2119-07-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning show your white count is coming down—from 12.6 to 10.9—so the antibiotics are helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2119-07-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Is my kidney function okay? I’m worried about that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2119-07-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine is up a bit to 4.3, but that’s expected. You’re still on dialysis three times a week. The nephrology team increased your cinacalcet to 60 mg twice daily to help control your PTH and slow the calciphylaxis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2119-07-14 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember they said I might need surgery on my parathyroid glands. Is that still the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2119-07-14 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Outpatient surgery is still recommended. We’ll follow up with the surgeon once you’re stable. For now, we’re focusing on infection control and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re getting ready to discharge you to the extended care facility. You’ll finish a 7-day course of oral clindamycin and ciprofloxacin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I need to follow up with dermatology for the injections?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We couldn’t schedule it yet, but if you don’t hear from them in two business days, call the clinic directly. Also, keep taking your oxycodone as needed for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I really want to switch dialysis centers. The one I’m at isn’t good to me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ve noted that. The care team will help you explore other options. Your health and comfort matter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel a bit better. The pain isn’t gone, but it’s more manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good progress. Keep up with wound care, take your meds, and follow up with your doctors. You’re doing the right things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure I do. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2119-07-14 16:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2119-07-13 20:48:00",
